      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Parathyroid (PTH) exploration surgery carries the risk of developing post-operative thyroiditis due to vigorous manual manipulation of the thyroid gland during surgery. Post-operative thyroiditis has a wide spectrum of clinical manifestations. However, it remains underreported. Here, we describe a case of post-operative transient thyroiditis in a 33-year-old male who developed 3\u2009days after parathyroidectomy for PTH hyperplasia. We review the limited literature regarding this interesting entity."},
